Significant changes made in this fork (from 2026-06-14 onward):

  - Replaced Termy's unauthenticated localhost WebSocket transport with
    OS-authenticated transports: a Windows named pipe (per-user DACL), a Unix
    domain socket (mode 0600 inside a per-user 0700 directory) on macOS and
    Linux, and a 256-bit capability-token authenticated WebSocket as a
    fallback.

  - Added a daemon-owned session model so terminal sessions survive an
    Obsidian reload: bounded output replay, reattach by session id, orphan
    timeouts, and re-discovery after a full reload.

  - Changed server-binary distribution to fetch only from this project's own
    GitHub release host (removing the third-party binary host), with build
    provenance attestation and SHA-256 hashes pinned in the plugin bundle.

  - Renamed the product from Termy to Scoria (plugin id, server binary,
    transport and file names, interface text, icon). Termy's history stays in
    CHANGELOG.md and in the git history.

  - Added a terminal "[[" wiki-link autocomplete. The UI/state class in
    src/services/terminal/wikilinkAutocomplete.ts is adapted from
    lean-obsidian-terminal (https://github.com/sdkasper/lean-obsidian-terminal),
    MIT licensed, itself ported from internetvin/internetvin-terminal
    (MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Vin Verma). The MIT permission notice for that
    original code is retained below. Adaptations: host-injected vault/insertion
    callbacks (no direct Obsidian App dependency), standard DOM, and the
    note-preview pane omitted.

